      "side": 1,
      "message": "Yes, eventually we should have native zephyr implementation for power button, option 1 is the goal. To have power button to work, power_button_x86.c needs to be included, it has dependency on a few things, chipset, system, hook, etc. It will takes some time to have all of those in zephyr code.\n\nTo have native power sequencing fully functional, power button is required, so we plan to use legacy EC code for now. Though the chipset related functions should come from zephyr power sequencing code. chipset_exit_hard_off() is implemented in this CL, chipset_in_state() are implemented in CL:3381901, many other places are calling chipset_in_state() too.  we need to have some configuration for those to be used by non-zephyr files. I have issue tracker b:214509787. In this way, option 3 is best for short term solution.",
